<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fidel Castro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1926">1926</a>–<a href="/years/2016">2016</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fidel Castro was a Cuban revolutionary who led the 26th of July Movement against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dictatorship">dictatorship</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fulgencio-batista">Fulgencio Batista</a>, attacking the Moncada barracks in 1953 and waging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-maestra">Sierra Maestra</a> after 1956. He took power in January 1959, aligned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> and built a one-party communist state, ruling as prime minister and president until handing power to his brother Raúl in 2008.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fidel-castro.jpg" alt="Fidel Castro" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown (Mondadori Publishers) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fidel_Castro_1950s_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In <b>Fidel Castro</b>’s Havana Declaration of 1979 its purpose was to ensure “the national independence, sovereignty, territorial integrity and security of non-aligned countries” in their struggle against imperialism, colonialism, neo-colonialism, racism and foreign aggression, occupation or domination, and against great power and bloc politics.</blockquote><a href="/movement/non-aligned-movement">Non-Aligned Movement · Aims</a></li><li><blockquote>A CIA-trained brigade of some 1,400 Cuban exiles landed in southern Cuba to overthrow <b>Fidel Castro</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/april-17">17 April in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Dictator Fulgencio Batista fled Havana in the early hours, handing victory to <b>Fidel Castro</b>'s guerrillas.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/january-1">1 January in history</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Fidel Castro</b> led some 160 rebels against the Moncada Barracks in Santiago de Cuba.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/july-26">26 July in history</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Fidel Castro's</b> 26th of July Movement overthrew Fulgencio Batista, who fled on 1 January 1959.</blockquote><a href="/state/republic-of-cuba">Republic of Cuba</a></li></ul></section>
